Agent service — the one roadmap #agents #plan

The single sequenced plan to finish the cloud Nexus **agent service**. The destination
is the ORIGINAL goal: **Waldo + the specialists (deck/video/research) doing real work
on your nexus — planning, scheduling, orchestrating sub-agents, filing issues, all
managed in the Studio.** Everything below is sequenced so each stage *unlocks* the next;
the infra prereqs exist only to make the agentic features real. Decisions live in
[[design]]; this is the execution order. We follow it stage by stage, top to bottom.

## Stage 0 — DONE (the spine, so we don't re-walk it)

Built + verified this run: default agents (`waldo`/`deck`/`research`) register + run by
name; durable **Runs** + SSE streaming + Studio Runs view; **task management + planning**
(Plan-with-Waldo → assigned subtasks → dispatch→run); **issue store + failure model**
(failed run auto-files an attributed issue); **scheduling** backend (agent runs on
cron/interval, re-armed on boot); **jj substrate** (Option B, gitlink-colocate over the
bare) + **attribution** + the **change-log in Activity**; the **per-agent worktree
primitive** (`Nexus.JJ.workspace_add/commit/forget` — isolated real FS, validated).

## Stage 1 — Agents write to the workspace (THE LINCHPIN) ✅ DONE  · unlocked 2,3,4

DONE + verified e2e: a workspace-scoped run mounts a jj worktree as the agent's real-FS
`/work`; bash gained `>`/`>>` redirection so agents author files naturally; on success the
edits seal as an attributed commit on `agent/<name>`; worktree forgotten, commits persist.
Proven: `Cloud.agent_run(workspace=myws, deck, 'echo … > pitch.work')` → `pitch.work`
committed to `agent/deck`. Gated by `jj-substrate` (off = ephemeral scratch). Commits:
`4bb1fc1c` (runtime) + `a9ebd513` (cloud).

Wire the validated worktree primitive into the run loop so a dispatched agent produces
**real, committed, attributed file changes** — the jj-FIFO + undo default, end to end.

1. Thread `workspace` (+ tenant, branch) through `Nexus.Agent.run_named`/`run` and the
   cloud `do_run`/dispatch path (today the run is workspace-blind).
2. For a workspace-scoped run, mount a `jj workspace add` worktree as the run's VFS
   (point `Nexus.Agent.Vfs`/the wasmtime `--dir` preopen at the real worktree, not the
   scratch temp). Guest sees only `/work`; writes hit real files.
3. After the run, `workspace_commit` (author = the agent) → the agent's branch
   (`agent/<name>` for the PR path, or `main` for the simple FIFO default).
4. `workspace_forget` cleanup (commits persist). Surface the change in Activity (the
   `workspace.change` event already exists).
5. Verify e2e: dispatch deck on a real workspace → a committed `.work` file appears,
   attributed, `jj undo`-able. Files touched: `agent.ex`, `agent/bash.ex`/`vfs.ex`,
   cloud `do_run`. (bd: agent→workspace-branch-write PREREQ)

## Stage 2 — Specialists do their real jobs (THE ORIGINAL ASK)  · needs 1 · IN PROGRESS

Now that agents can write the tree (Stage 1), make the specialists produce real artifacts.
Prereq landed: **heredoc** support in the agent shell (`cat > f <<EOF … EOF`) so agents
author multi-line `.work` files.
- **Deck** ✅ — real `.work` deck surface (Reveal.js `client` island + `<section>` slides),
  committed to `decks/<slug>/`. Verified e2e: a 4-slide investor deck committed to
  `agent/deck` with the island + reveal.js wired.
- **Research** ✅ (refined) — organized `research/<slug>/` repo: one `.work` note per
  sub-topic with `[[backlinks]]` + `#tags` + an `index.work` map; same proven
  heredoc-authoring path as Deck. (Recurring gather→organize as `flow`+`trigger` = later.)
- **Video** ⬜ — BLOCKED: the wasm-video package isn't a compiled agent kit yet (only
  `coreutils`+`web` are). Needs wasm-video wired as a kit + a render-job path. (bd: wb-luce)

## Stage 3 — Git-backed store + the Studio surfaces  · needs 1

- Move **tasks/issues to git-backed `.work`** at `<ws>/.nexus/{tasks,issues}/<id>.work`
  (source of truth, jj-covered), SQLite as the derived index (write-through + rebuild).
  (bd: wb-xxks)
- **Studio buildout**: Schedules panel + Issues panel (we have the backends); fold
  schedule into the Tasks board; durable agent sessions; sub-agent runs collapsed under
  the parent. (bd: wb-980e + Schedules-UI)

## Stage 4 — Workflow config + PRs/GitHub  · needs 1,3

- **Per-subtree workflow config** (`.work`-declared): default = jj FIFO + undo (CRDT);
  opt-in review policy (a reviewer/**merger** agent on a `pr.opened` hook, routed
  agent-PR vs human-PR), branch policy (prod vs dev gate), validation (`flow`/`check`
  before merge). (bd: workflow-config-layer)
- **GitHub PR/issue API + fetch-back**: open a PR for an agent branch (link the nexus
  issue); opt-in promote a task to a GitHub Issue with status sync; pull merged PRs back
  (the bidirectional half). Uses the integrations GitHub token + native `git subtree`
  (the [[josh]] decision — no josh). (bd: github-pr-api)

## Stage 5 — Orchestration depth + production hardening  · needs 1,2

- **Sub-agent orchestration**: depth cap, grant narrowing, structured `.work` handoff
  docs, Studio sub-run tree. (The original "orchestrate + manage sub-agents".)
- **Cost/spend** metering + per-org caps (budget pause, upsell knob via `Nexus.Config`).
- **jj flag-flip** on the dogfood deploy (confirm jj is in the runtime image) + Undo/op
  surfacing; multi-tenant schedule re-arm fan-out; fix the agent `model`-field bug
  (bd: wb-bg5z).

## The through-line (don't lose the forest)

Stage 1 is the one linchpin; 2 is the original goal made real; 3–4 make it
collaborative + production-safe; 5 is depth. Tasks → runs → issues → schedules → changes
are already **one fabric**; Stage 1 connects agents' actual file work into that fabric,
and the rest is surfacing + policy. We execute top-to-bottom, committing each stage green.
